Recipe Changes

Purpose

Recipe changes are used to enforce the progression defined by the pack.

Recipes should create meaningful technological requirements rather than simply increasing crafting costs.

Every major recipe change must have a reason connected to progression, integration, automation, resource management, or technological advancement.

Recipe Philosophy

Recipes should represent technological development.

Early recipes should remain simple and accessible.

As progression advances, recipes should become increasingly dependent on:

Advanced materials

Industrial processing

Specialized machines

Power infrastructure

Cross-mod components

Automation

Higher technological tiers

Recipe complexity should create a reason to build infrastructure.

Recipes should not become complicated only for the sake of being complicated.

Starting Point Recipes

Vanilla progression remains available at the beginning of the game.

Basic tools, weapons, armor, furnaces, crafting tables, and other fundamental survival equipment should remain accessible.

Modded technology should not be immediately available.

The first technological recipes should introduce the Primitive Age.

Primitive Age Recipes

Primitive recipes introduce the first technological components.

Recipes should require basic processed materials and primitive industrial infrastructure.

The Primitive Age should establish the resources and components required to enter the Steam Age.

Steam Age Recipes

Steam Age recipes introduce the first major industrial systems.

Steam-powered machines, Create infrastructure, GregTech components, and Modern Industrialization systems should begin interacting.

Steam should become the primary solution for early industrial production.

LV Recipes

LV recipes introduce electrical technology.

LV machines and components should require materials and infrastructure established during the Steam Age.

Electrical infrastructure should become necessary for continued progression.

MV Recipes

MV recipes should require LV progression and increasingly advanced materials.

Recipes should introduce more complex processing chains and larger production requirements.

HV Recipes

HV recipes should represent a significant increase in industrial scale.

Recipes should require advanced materials, complex processing, and stable MV infrastructure.

Automation should become increasingly important.

EV Recipes

EV recipes should require advanced industrial materials, chemical processing, and HV infrastructure.

EV components should require multiple stages of production.

Recipes should encourage large-scale automated factories.

IV Recipes

IV recipes should require EV infrastructure and extremely advanced materials.

Complex components should combine materials and processing systems from multiple mods.

IV should represent a major increase in industrial complexity.

LuV Recipes

LuV recipes should require IV progression and advanced industrial infrastructure.

Recipes should introduce extremely advanced materials, components, and processing chains.

Automation should be strongly encouraged.

ZPM Recipes

ZPM recipes should require LuV progression.

Recipes should represent extremely advanced technology and require substantial industrial infrastructure.

Production should generally be automated before large-scale ZPM progression.

UV Recipes

UV recipes should require ZPM progression and extreme industrial infrastructure.

Recipes should require advanced materials, complex processing, and very high power capacity.

UV should represent the highest levels of conventional industrial technology.

UHV Recipes

UHV recipes should require UV progression.

Recipes should represent the extreme end of conventional industrial development.

Production should require highly optimized factories, advanced logistics, enormous power infrastructure, and complex multi-stage processing.

Cross-Mod Recipes

Important components should sometimes combine systems from different mods.

Examples include:

GregTech materials processed through Modern Industrialization

Mekanism chemical processing used for advanced components

Create machinery used for mechanical processing

AE2 components used for advanced logistics

Create Aeronautics components requiring industrial materials

Create Big Cannons components requiring advanced manufacturing

Cross-mod recipes must have a clear progression purpose.

They should not exist only to increase crafting difficulty.

GregTech Recipe Integration

GregTech recipes should remain the primary structure for technological progression.

Where necessary, existing GregTech recipes may be modified to connect them with other systems.

Higher-tier components should require appropriate previous-tier infrastructure.

Modern Industrialization Recipe Integration

Modern Industrialization recipes should be integrated into the main progression.

MI machines and components should use appropriate materials and technological requirements.

MI must not create an alternative route that bypasses GregTech progression.

Create Recipe Integration

Create recipes should be modified when necessary to connect mechanical technology with industrial progression.

Create should remain useful for mechanical automation, logistics, transportation, and specialized processing.

Create recipes should not provide unintended shortcuts to advanced industrial materials.

Mekanism Recipe Integration

Mekanism recipes should be integrated with the technological progression.

Advanced Mekanism systems may require materials and components from higher industrial tiers.

Mekanism should remain valuable for chemical processing and specialized industrial systems without replacing the main progression.

AE2 Recipe Integration

AE2 progression should be gated appropriately.

Advanced storage, crafting, automation, and logistics components should require suitable technological infrastructure.

AE2 should simplify logistics rather than simplify the technological progression itself.

Progression-Breaking Recipes

Recipes that bypass progression must be removed or modified.

Examples include:

Early access to advanced materials

Early access to high-tier machines

Alternative recipes that bypass required processing

Cheap access to advanced power systems

Recipes that bypass technological tiers

Recipes that provide endgame materials too early

Recipes that allow one mod to completely replace another mod's intended progression role

The goal is not to remove useful alternatives.

The goal is to prevent unintended progression shortcuts.

Recipe Scaling

Recipe difficulty should increase alongside technological progression.

Higher-tier recipes may require:

More materials

More processing stages

More advanced machines

Higher-tier components

Cross-mod components

Greater power requirements

Automated production

However, material quantity alone should not be the primary method of increasing difficulty.

Automation should become the intended solution to large production requirements.

Endgame Recipes

Endgame recipes should require extensive infrastructure.

Advanced components should combine multiple technological systems.

Post-endgame recipes should require resources and infrastructure accumulated throughout the entire progression.

ProjectE and Avaritia recipes should represent major progression milestones rather than ordinary crafting recipes.

Implementation

Recipe modifications will be implemented primarily through KubeJS.

Recipes will be organized according to progression tiers and technological systems.

Recipe changes should be documented so that the GuideME handbook can explain important progression requirements.

All custom recipes should be tested for:

Correct progression requirements

Correct materials

Correct machine requirements

Correct power requirements

Correct cross-mod dependencies

Compatibility with automation

Compatibility with multiplayer

No unintended progression shortcuts
